  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Emergency lifesaving Health, Nutrition, WASH and Protection support for vulnerable populations affected by adverse effects of El Ni&#xf1;o in South Central Somalia - Phase 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribute to reducing the risk of morbidity and mortality associated with the Deyr rain-related floods and disease outbreaks among vulnerable populations in Balcad, Dollow, Galkacyo, Wanlaweyn, and Kismayo districts. Through the deployment of community-based integrated health, nutrition, protection, and WASH teams as well as community health workers (CHW), the consortium partners will set out to achieve the following objectives: 1. Increase access to a package of integrated life-saving emergency health services2. Increase access to preventive and curative nutrition services3. Increase access to protection services, especially targeting women and children in the affected districts4. Improve access to safe water, sanitation, and waste management5. Crises response</narrative>
  </description>
